NOTICE: This is a custom, source-available, noncommercial research license.
It is NOT an OSI-approved open-source license. Legal review is recommended.

1. Scope. "Materials" means the source code, model parameters, model
checkpoints, documentation, and other files located in the
releases/nnm-49 directory when distributed by the copyright holder under
this license. This license does not automatically cover other repository
directories or third-party materials.

2. Noncommercial research grant. Subject to these terms, the copyright
holder grants each recipient a worldwide, nonexclusive, royalty-free,
revocable only for breach license to access, use, copy, run, study, modify,
and redistribute the Materials and modifications solely for noncommercial
research, education, and evaluation. Recipients may publish research
findings and benchmark results, including negative results.

3. Conditions on redistribution. Redistributed Materials and modifications
must retain this license, copyright notices, and attribution to the original
NNM-49 project, identify material modifications, and must not suggest
endorsement by the copyright holder. No recipient may sublicense commercial
rights.

4. Commercial activity. "Commercial Use" means use of the Materials or
modifications primarily intended for commercial advantage, including
incorporation into a paid product or service, paid access, commercial
deployment, or research performed on behalf of a commercial customer.
A commercial entity may perform purely internal, noncommercial evaluation
solely to determine whether to seek a commercial license, provided that
the evaluation is not deployed or used to deliver commercial services.

5. Notification and separate agreement. Before beginning Commercial Use,
the prospective user must notify the copyright holder by opening a GitHub
issue in https://github.com/josh003blip/nnm-49 with the subject
"NNM-49 commercial licensing inquiry", or by another contact channel
publicly designated by the copyright holder. The notice should describe
the proposed use and a means of reply, without disclosing confidential
business information in a public issue. The parties may then discuss
commercial licensing terms. NOTIFICATION ALONE DOES NOT AUTHORIZE
COMMERCIAL USE. Commercial Use is prohibited unless and until a separate
written agreement expressly permits it. The copyright holder is under no
obligation to offer or agree to commercial terms.

6. Contributions. This license does not transfer ownership of a
recipient's independently authored modifications. Recipients must have
the rights needed to distribute any contributions they submit. The
copyright holder does not receive ownership of contributions merely
because they were made using the Materials.

7. No trademark or patent grant. This license grants no trademark rights
and no express patent license. Nothing in this license limits rights
that recipients already possess under applicable law.

8. Termination. Rights under this license terminate automatically upon
a material breach that is not cured within 30 days after the recipient
receives written notice. Commercial activity without the required
separate agreement is unauthorized from its outset.

9. Disclaimer. TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, THE
MATERIALS ARE PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS
OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE,
AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW,
THE COPYRIGHT HOLDER IS NOT LIABLE FOR INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL,
CONSEQUENTIAL, OR EXEMPLARY DAMAGES ARISING FROM USE OF THE MATERIALS.

10. Reservation. All rights not expressly granted are reserved.
